rrent law but that  we would no longer get and hasn't been  budgeted and thus would increase the  deficit something that Republicans claim  they don't want this has gone beyond Pat  simply economics into immorality and  kleptocracy by the minority for the  minority that fills their pockets yes  speaking just on the back pay for a  second I thought it was just Trump who  tried to avoid paying people who worked  for him it turns out it's a good portion  of the Republican Party and also I would  go a step further I don't think that the  federal contractors are just owed back  pay I think they're owed like three or  four percent interest on top of that if  you're late on your taxes  you have to pay interest on it you'll  get penalized you end up having to pay  more than you initially owed I think I  think we also owe those federal  contractors not only for the time that  they've missed but also a little  something extra yeah that's something  that's that's being discussed which is  the idea that if you ended up having to  I don't know take a loan out in order to  make your mortgage payment or pay rent  or buy groceries or whatever as the  shutdown was going on as a result of  Donald Trump's temper tantrum shouldn't  you be compensated for that if you are  paying interest on a loan because of the  shutdown shouldn't you have that made up  to you and I think that that ship that  ship hasn't it's not that that ship has  sailed  that ship doesn't exist that ship hasn't  been built that ship is just an idea  not even in a boat yard yet to take the  the ship analogy to its full conclusion  it's the Gilded Age kleptocracy swamp I  don't know what to call it but we need  to end it in 2020 today's program is  sponsored in part by Blink accom slash  Pakman if you've not already heard about  blink Asst it's amazing it's an app for  your phone tablet or web browser and  what they do is they take nonfiction  books popular nonfiction critically  acclaimed nonfiction they condense the